food options are limited for many in  Lebanon affected by the collapse of its  economy  many items are now crossed off from  their shopping lists  I used to buy three or four kilos of  tomatoes now it's one or even half a  kilo everything changed I can't afford  meat or chicken we are only buying  Essentials  the collapse of the local currency has  affected people's purchasing power the  world food program says the average  salary in Lebanon now covers 24 percent  of basic food needs  it's helping feed one in three Lebanese  for the past two years the situation is  catastrophic the currency's devaluation  hurt us we used to eat two meals a day  now we barely can afford one and it's  potatoes most of the time we spend it  three times more than our income  for goods have since flooded the market  but despite that food prices increased  30 percent this year and more than one  thousand five hundred percent since the  economic crisis began in 2019.  we used to buy goods from the west but  people couldn't pay one dollar for a  chocolate bar now we import from turkey  and Syria because it's cheaper  the political class blamed for decades  of bad policies and Corruption is  failing to address the crisis the  situation could get worse as the country  heads to what could be an extended  political vacuum  Parliament failed to elect a successor  to president michelown who leaves office  at the end of the month it won't be the  first time the country has been without  a leader but this time around there's  likely to be no government to take on  executive powers  this is no longer a middle-income  country and there's little social  justice many like Ahmed simul have no  social protection and are forced to find  any way they can to survive the new  reality Beirut
 

